      "body": "## Motivation\n\nAdaptive speculative decoding currently falls back to static parameters when two-batch overlap is enabled because rebuilding an adaptive target runtime state bypasses the `TboAttnBackend` wrapper.\n\nRefs #23705.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Build adaptive target attention backends with the configured TBO wrapper.\n- Share the same TBO-aware backend factory between normal startup and adaptive runtime-state construction.\n- Remove the adaptive-spec TBO compatibility guard.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis initial PR targets EP TBO without attention DP. Attention-DP plus TBO is intentionally left out because adaptive DP requires cross-rank tier consensus and is tracked as a separate roadmap item.\n\n## Testing\n\nNot run yet. Opening as a draft for scope and design feedback.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39896049450](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39896049450)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39896049313](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39896049313)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39896049229](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39896049229)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
